  "details": "I think the current basic nature of shield settings are too vague. Certain things can be on or off and that's it. \n\nAvatar stats list many attributes such as material count, poly count and number of particles. Yet none of this can be controlled by shield settings.\n\nI'd really like to see fine controls be added for every aspect of an avatar. Eg, I could set my shield to hide any avatar over 200,000 polys, 5 particle systems and 8 meshes (this is an example). So before an avatar loads, the stats are downloaded, then the decision to load or not to load is based on if it violates any user set limits.\n\nThis would allow each user to decide their own acceptable levels of avatar features. To avoid confusing players, this system could be in an advanced button within shield settings.\n\nTo kinda sum this up in a few sentences. Setting hard limits to certain features would prevent most crashers. Set a poly and mesh limit, 95% of crashers now don't load. People who understand the settings would be able to decide what limits they think is best.\n\nAn argument against this could be that vrchat server side checks avatars to ensure they don't reach limits. My response would be why do multi million poly meshes that set everyone to 1fps still work then? If we could set our own limit, the issue goes way. The server side checks block the most extreme examples, but the top end of what they allow is still very harmful. \n\nLowering the limit wouldn't be the solution as some legit avatars need high limits. So user settable limits would be my solution.\n\nSide note, I believe what I just suggested actually used to be a mod before EAC was a thing.",
